{#
    Screenshots of the extension, linked from the maintainer's own repository.

    Never hosted here. §4.3 prefers linking to hosting, and screenshots are the
    vendor's material rather than ours — a code licence covers the software, not the
    marketing images, so copying them would be the one part of this needing
    permission we do not have.

    Every URL was restricted at collection time to a host the extension's own forge
    serves. Sampled READMEs also link to imgur, giphy, cloudinary and vendors' own
    marketing servers; those are dropped rather than quietly widening consent that
    was given for "icons from their forges".

    The section stays hidden until the reader allows remote media. Unlike an icon
    there is nothing to fall back on — a gallery with nothing in it is not a gallery
    — so it removes itself rather than showing grey rectangles to somebody who
    declined.
#}
{% set images = extension_gallery(extension) %}
{% if images|length %}
    <section class="panel" data-remote-media-target="gallery" hidden aria-label="Screenshots">
        <h2>Screenshots</h2>
        <p class="subtle gallery-note">
            Published by the maintainer in their own repository, and loaded directly from
            {{ extension_icon_host(extension) ?? 'the source repository' }} — extdir neither
            stores nor serves them.
        </p>

        <div class="rail" data-controller="rail">
            <div class="rail-track gallery-track" data-rail-target="track" tabindex="0"
                 role="group" aria-label="Screenshots of {{ extension.label }}">
                {% for image in images %}
                    {# Opens the full-size original on the forge rather than in a
                       lightbox: the file is theirs and stays theirs, and a new tab
                       puts where it came from in the address bar. #}
                    <a class="shot" href="{{ image }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"
                       data-remote-media-target="slot"
                       data-remote-media-url="{{ image }}"
                       data-remote-media-class="shot-img"
                       aria-label="Screenshot {{ loop.index }} of {{ images|length }}, opens on {{ extension_icon_host(extension) ?? 'the source repository' }}">
                        <span class="shot-index" aria-hidden="true">{{ loop.index }}</span>
                    </a>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>

            <button class="rail-nav rail-nav--prev" type="button" hidden
                    data-rail-target="prev" data-action="rail#prev" aria-label="Scroll to previous screenshots">‹</button>
            <button class="rail-nav rail-nav--next" type="button" hidden
                    data-rail-target="next" data-action="rail#next" aria-label="Scroll to more screenshots">›</button>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}
